<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Library on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/library/</link><description>Recent content in Library on Tech Insights: AI &amp; Cloud</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:09:21 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/tags/library/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Chroma.js Library Provides Comprehensive Color Conversion and Scaling Capabilities</title><link>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/chroma-js-library-provides-comprehensive-color-conversion-and-scaling-capabilities/</link><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:09:21 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://shoubhikbanerjee.github.io/blog/p/chroma-js-library-provides-comprehensive-color-conversion-and-scaling-capabilities/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/617518?v=4" alt="Featured image of post Chroma.js Library Provides Comprehensive Color Conversion and Scaling Capabilities" /&gt;&lt;h1 id="chromajs-library-provides-comprehensive-color-conversion-and-scaling-capabilities"&gt;Chroma.js Library Provides Comprehensive Color Conversion and Scaling Capabilities
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chroma.js is a small-ish zero-dependency JavaScript library for all kinds of color conversions and color scales. It can be installed via npm with &lt;code&gt;npm install chroma-js&lt;/code&gt; and imported using &lt;code&gt;import chroma from &amp;quot;chroma-js&amp;quot;;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-overview"&gt;🔍 Overview
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The library supports various color operations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;chroma('#D4F880').darken().hex();&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;#a1c550&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;scale = chroma.scale(['white', 'red']);&lt;/code&gt; creates a color scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;scale(0.5).hex();&lt;/code&gt; returns &lt;code&gt;#FF7F7F&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-key-features"&gt;⚙️ Key Features
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chroma.js offers advanced interpolation methods and customization options:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lab/Lch Interpolation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Provides better color interpolation than RGB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Custom Domains&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supports custom data domains for scaling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Quantiles&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Offers quantile-based color scaling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Color Brewer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Integrates Color Brewer palettes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Logarithmic Scales&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supports logarithmic color scale domains&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Example usage:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-javascript" data-lang="javascript"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chroma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;white&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;red&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;lab&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chroma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;white&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;red&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;myValues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;quantiles&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chroma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;lightyellow&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;navy&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;log&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The library is written by Gregor Aisch and released under the BSD license. Documentation is available both as an interactive version at &lt;a class="link" href="http://gka.github.io/chroma.js/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;http://gka.github.io/chroma.js/&lt;/a&gt; and as a static version on GitHub.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-availability"&gt;🚀 Availability
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Developers can access Chroma.js through multiple channels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Download &lt;code&gt;chroma.min.js&lt;/code&gt; directly from GitHub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the hosted version on unpkg.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install via npm for Node.js applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use with SASS through the chromatic-sass package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-development-details"&gt;💡 Development Details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;To contribute to Chroma.js:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clone the repository: &lt;code&gt;git clone git@github.com:gka/chroma.js.git&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install dev dependencies and compile CoffeeScript source files: &lt;code&gt;npm run build&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run tests: &lt;code&gt;npm test&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add tests for new features in the &lt;code&gt;/test&lt;/code&gt; folder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note that versions prior to 0.4 were released under the GPL license.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#JavaScript #Color #Visualization #Library #RGB #Lab&lt;/p&gt;
